                <pb facs="0275" n="261" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg261"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The Secretary of State in a letter to British Chargé Balfour, dated July 25,
                    1947, and British Ambassador Inverchapel, in his reply of October 9, 1947,
                    agreed on arrangements whereby the United Kingdom would continue to furnish
                    military equipment and supplies to the Greek armed forces and the United States
                    obligated itself to pay for such arrivals after May 22, 1947; for texts, see
                    Department of State Treaties and Other International Acts Series No. 1718, or 61
                    Stat. (pt. 4) 3763.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
